# kde-macos-config -- pinned dock launchers
#
# One app per line, in dock order. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# To remove an app from the dock, delete its line here and re-run ./apply.sh --
# unpinning it by hand does not stick, because layout.js rewrites the whole list
# on every apply.
#
# An id is only pinned if its .desktop file is actually installed; anything
# missing is skipped and reported during apply, so a stale id can never turn into
# a generic "Unknown application" tile. Separate alternatives for the same app
# with "|": the first one that is installed wins, so an app is pinned at most
# once. Use that where distros and third-party repos disagree on the id.

org.kde.dolphin.desktop                  # Files
org.kde.konsole.desktop                  # Terminal
org.mozilla.firefox.desktop              # Web
com.google.Chrome.desktop                # Web
com.microsoft.VSCode.desktop|code.desktop # VS Code (the RPM ships the long id)
